From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exynos6694 <azsx6694@naver.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:50:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Local wireless play: online by default through NX2Apple's
 relay, one room per game

The launcher's "Local wireless play" switch (DM_COOP=auto) alone now reaches players on other networks:
with none of DM_COOP_INTERNET, DM_COOP_RELAY and DM_COOP_JOIN set, coop_env_node turns on internet play
through COOP_RELAY_BUILTIN (158.180.89.88:47610, the coop-relay in NX2Apple's multiplayer/server) and
uses the game's own room, coop_room_for_title: 80 bits of SHA-256 over a tag and the title ID, which a
new coop_hooks.title gives (hle_offline.c: the profile's program ID). Nobody types a code or an address.
One host at a time per game, and anyone with the title ID can compute the room. DM_COOP_ROOM gives a
private room, DM_COOP_RELAY another relay, DM_COOP_INTERNET=0 the LAN play with DNS-SD as before.
-DCOOP_RELAY_BUILTIN='""' builds without a built-in relay.

t_coop_loop: the room is stable, valid and differs per game, and DM_COOP=auto alone picks the relay.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: The fork's own relay server as the default for local wireless play, so the launcher switch alone plays over the internet
Issue: none yet (exynos6694/NX2Apple-muti feature/local-wireless)
